52: 
53: At the I2 cusp use F31's literal line graph
54: \(h_j=\lceil j/2\rceil\), \(h_{j+2}=h_j+1\).
55: The forward +G source shift is \(j\mapsto j+1\). After multiplying
56: \(U\) by an integral base monomial, its line multiplier has valuation
57: zero. The two actual graph defects are
58: \[
59:  h_j-h_{j+1}=-1\quad(j\ {
60: m even}),\qquad
61:  h_j-h_{j+1}=0\quad(j\ {
62: m odd}).                              \tag{OS.4}
63: \]
64: Thus the pole divisor is \(-C_0\). This includes both node charts,
65: because their endpoint graph defects determine the two fibre-coordinate
66: monomials. The third translated norm has divisor \(-2C_0-C_1\).
67: The maps \(B_0^{-1}\) and \(U^3\) cover the same translation,
68: so their ratio is a rational base function
69: \[
70:  \rho=B_0^{-1}/U^3,\qquad \operatorname{ord}_{q=0}\rho=1.         \tag{OS.5}
71: \]
72: The ratio is constant on each compact generic elliptic fibre. With another
73: whole-fibre normalization of \(U\), the last order is \(1-3e\),
74: which is the same exact congruence needed below.
